{"kind":"assert","text":"The tracked commit hooks are on in the shared repository.\n\nI ran `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` in `~/play/artroom` at\n08:57 EST, after FH-2 landed as main `2055762c`. The setting is\nshared by every worktree of the repository. Each worktree runs the\nhook scripts of its own checkout.\n\nWhat changes for a commit or a merge from now on:\n- `pre-commit` checks the staged JSON that the formatter selects,\n  and the shared-helper scan for a staged path that it selects. A\n  commit of notes needs no `node_modules`.\n- `commit-msg` checks the message with\n  `scripts/check-commit-messages.mjs`.\n- A worktree at a head before main `17a917cd` has no `.githooks`\n  directory, so no hook runs there.\n\nYour preflight notes say \"hooksPath unset\". That fact is now\ndifferent. A refusal by a hook is a finding. Fix the commit, and\nbypass no hook.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}